│ patch_description        │ The edge-count strategy currently chooses adjacent codewords with a separation of only    │
│                          │ about 2.5 standard deviations of the noisy edge count. This produces a substantial        │
│                          │ adjacent-class confusion probability, and because 100 independent predictions are scored  │
│                          │ exponentially through \(0.9^E\), reducing errors is much more valuable than the moderate  │
│                          │ increase in N.                                                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ For an interior codeword, a normal approximation gives error probability approximately    │
│                          │ \(2\Phi(-K/2)\), where K is the adjacent mean separation in standard deviations.          │
│                          │ Maximizing the expected score proxy \((1-0.1p)^{100}/N\), while noting that N grows       │
│                          │ approximately linearly with K, gives an optimum near K=4.8 rather than 2.5. This change   │
│                          │ increases graph size only when the edge-count strategy is selected, but greatly improves  │
│                          │ robustness against noise.                                                                 │
