│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ degree_profile_decoder                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ The edge-count strategy currently discards almost all information in the received graph:  │
│                          │ it distinguishes codewords only by the total number of edges. Although vertex labels are  │
│                          │ shuffled, the sorted degree sequence remains available and is a permutation-invariant     │
│                          │ fingerprint of the randomly generated code graph.                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Store each transmitted graph's degree sequence. For a query, compare its centered sorted  │
│                          │ degree profile with the expected noisy profile of every candidate. Centering removes the  │
│                          │ component already represented by total edge count, avoiding excessive double-counting.    │
│                          │ The resulting score combines the existing edge-count likelihood proxy with a              │
│                          │ degree-profile residual normalized by the approximate degree noise variance.              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This is especially useful for low-to-medium noise cases where the edge-count strategy     │
│                          │ uses a moderately large N: graphs with nearby edge counts can have distinguishable degree │
│                          │ distributions after shuffling.                                                            │
│ num_applied              │ 5                                                                                         │
