│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ cost_aware_n_selection                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the fixed separation heuristic for the edge-count strategy with a direct search   │
│                          │ over all valid graph sizes.  The score has a very strong nonlinear dependence on the      │
│                          │ probability of an error across 100 queries, while also dividing the result by N.          │
│                          │ Therefore the best N is not generally characterized by one fixed K value.                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ For every candidate N, estimate the classification error of the actual equally spaced     │
│                          │ edge-count code.  Each boundary between adjacent codewords contributes a Gaussian tail    │
│                          │ probability based on its true integer edge-count spacing, the expected post-noise         │
│                          │ spacing, and the exact edge-count noise variance L*epsilon*(1-epsilon).  The estimated    │
│                          │ expected score multiplier is (1-0.1*p_error)^100 / N, matching the expectation of 0.9^E   │
│                          │ for 100 independent queries.  This also accounts for rounding of codeword edge counts,    │
│                          │ which is relevant for small N.                                                            │
