│ patch_description        │ The large-N branch currently encodes only through total edge count, despite spending many │
│                          │ vertices on each codeword. Replace random graphs with nested dense-core (colex) graphs,   │
│                          │ whose sorted degree sequences provide an additional permutation-invariant signature.      │
│                          │ Decode using the edge-count likelihood plus a conservatively weighted degree-spectrum     │
│                          │ residual. The degree term is centered so it captures shape rather than merely counting    │
│                          │ every edge twice, and it is normalized by the noise-induced per-vertex degree variance.   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This retains the robust edge-count channel while extracting useful information from the   │
│                          │ graph structure after vertex shuffling. Dense-core graphs make these degree signatures    │
│                          │ much more separated than the current uniformly random graphs.                             │
