│ patch_description        │ This redesign separates the solution into two encoder/decoder engines behind a common     │
│                          │ interactive controller.                                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ - For zero-noise cases, it uses a compact small-graph isomorphism codec. Graphs are       │
│                          │ selected greedily by permutation-invariant edit distance, then decoded through canonical  │
│                          │ graph masks.                                                                              │
│                          │ - For noisy cases, it uses a large 100-vertex invariant codec. Each codeword has a        │
│                          │ distinct edge count and a deterministic heterogeneous degree profile. Decoding combines   │
│                          │ the noise-corrected edge-count likelihood with a lower-weight sorted-degree signature     │
│                          │ likelihood.                                                                               │
│                          │ - The architecture removes shared mutable global graph state, encapsulates graph          │
│                          │ construction/decoding into classes, and makes the strategy selection and query loop       │
│                          │ straightforward.                                                                          │
