│ patch_description        │ This redesign separates the solution into two independent codecs selected by noise level: │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ - `ZeroNoiseCodec` builds unlabeled graph representatives through permutation-orbit       │
│                          │ enumeration, greedily chooses separated graph codewords, and decodes queries through a    │
│                          │ precomputed orbit-owner lookup table. This removes repeated graph-edit-distance searches  │
│                          │ during queries.                                                                           │
│                          │ - `EdgeCountCodec` uses a deterministic edge-count codebook for noisy cases. It selects   │
│                          │ `N` by evaluating the actual rounded count codebook and each message’s discrete decision  │
│                          │ boundaries, using a score-aligned expected objective.                                     │
│                          │ - The program is organized around codec classes with isolated construction, output, and   │
│                          │ decoding flows, improving maintainability and reducing global mutable state.              │
